\ The Fibonacci native-fallback bug's repro, end to end under the lock: the
\ string print, the `.` on a computed number, and the timing loop all compile
\ with no fallback, and the binary runs interpreter-free.
\
\ One change from the bug report's program: fib declares a fixnum output.
\ That annotation is load-bearing -- the freeze-time inference trusts it to
\ prove `.`'s parameter, which lets `.`'s standalone body monomorphize its
\ `inspect` and pass the lock. The fully-unannotated form still rejects,
\ pinned by fib_repro_unannotated_reject.1z.

fib-step: ( a b n -- result ) [
  dup 0 = [ drop drop ] [
    1 - [ swap over + ] dip fib-step
  ] if
] ;

fib: ( n -- result: fixnum ) [
  dup 2 < [ ] [
    0 1 <rot- fib-step
  ] if
] ;

repeat-fib: ( n -- ) [
  dup 0 = [ drop ] [
    1 - 30 fib drop repeat-fib
  ] if
] ;

"fib(30) = " print 30 fib .
5000 repeat-fib
